data-tex=\"\\operatorname{NormalOperator}_H(N)\">\\(\\operatorname{NormalOperator}_H(N)\\)</span> (normal-operator predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}operator\\text{-}explicit}\\vdash \\operatorname{NormalOperator}_S(N,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(N,H,H)\\land\\exists N^\\ast\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(N,N^\\ast,H,H)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(N^\\ast,H,H)\\land\\forall x\\in H\\;(N^\\ast(N(x))=N(N^\\ast(x)))\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}operator\\text{-}explicit}\\vdash \\operatorname{NormalOperator}_S(N,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(N,H,H)\\land\\exists N^\\ast\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(N,N^\\ast,H,H)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(N^\\ast,H,H)\\land\\forall x\\in H\\;(N^\\ast(N(x))=N(N^\\ast(x)))\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}operator\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash \\operatorname{NormalOperator}_H(N)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{NormalOperator}_S(N,H)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}operator\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash \\operatorname{NormalOperator}_H(N)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{NormalOperator}_S(N,H)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Normal operators have orthogonal spectral decompositions.</li>\n<li>The Hilbert carrier is now a public argument of the core predicate, and every composed operator application is guarded by a set-function graph.</li>\n<li>Self-adjoint and unitary operators are normal.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},